    "name": "island-core",
    "type": "registry:lib",
    "title": "Island core",
    "description": "The islandcn engine: a Dynamic Island-style pill for React with no animation library. Closed-form SwiftUI springs (response, dampingFraction, blendDuration) that retarget mid-flight, an activity stack (compact, minimal split, expanded, alerting updates, long-press, groups that show one activity at a time), an SVG shape with continuous corners (an arc eased into each edge, fitted to the simulator) and a metaball split, content that follows the shape and crossfades with blur and scale under a fixed sensor cutout, a dark-page keyline, IslandNumber and IslandProgress primitives that animate in-place updates, press and tap timing from touch-down, reduced-motion crossfades, and a pausable clock with devtools for frame-exact captures.",
    "docs": "Wrap your app in <IslandProvider>, render <Island /> at the top of a positioned container (or placement=\"viewport\"), and start activities with useIsland().start({ id, compact, minimal, expanded }). To have your coding agent build islands on this engine, add the islandcn skill: npx shadcn@latest add {{REGISTRY_URL}}/islandcn-skill.json",
